{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>To the place of which I spoke to you.</b> When He said: אַעֲלֶה אֶתְכֶם מֵעֳנִי מִצְרַיִם אֶל אֶרֶץ טוֹבָה וְגוֹ׳ (Exodus 3:17)." "<b>And on the day of My visitation.</b> When they add further sin, as with the spies." "<b>And I will visit upon them their sin.</b> This sin — and I will not add further punishment for it, as in וְאִם רָעָה תִּמָּצֵא בוֹ וָמֵת (I Kings 1:52). And so He indicated there in saying: עַד אָנָה יְנַאֲצֻנִי הָעָם הַזֶּה (Numbers 14:11), for since they repeat in their folly they are presumed likely to add further guilt, as the Sages, may their memory be for blessing, stated (Yoma 86a): once a person transgresses and repeats, it becomes permitted to him — that is, it becomes to him as though permitted."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {2 "The phrase עֲבוּר לוֹ is rendered as 'punishment for it,' reading עָבוּר in the sense of consequence/penalty; the idiom is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:53.153153309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}